1qf4|n|The art of composition; especially, elegant composition in prose. ; Oratory; the art of speaking with propriety, elegance, and force. ; Hence, artificial eloquence; fine language or declamation without conviction or earnest feeling. ; Fig. : The power of persuasion or attraction; that which allures or charms.	a:1jz0,70,3~1jz0,70,3
1qf5|a|Of or pertaining to rhetoric; according to, or exhibiting, rhetoric; oratorical; as, the rhetorical art; a rhetorical treatise; a rhetorical flourish.	j:jma,43,12~jma,43,12
